        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(shared): consolidate lazy import memoizers",
        "body": "Related: #98748\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a maintainability problem where lazy runtime imports repeatedly implement their own module-level promise cache, loader, retry, and reset behavior across core and bundled plugins. The consolidation report identified this as the largest duplicate utility family, but the initial PR migrated only one small caller batch.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMakes `createLazyPromiseLoader` the canonical single-flight promise owner, keeps `createLazyPromise` as its direct function form, and makes the higher-level lazy runtime helpers delegate to it. The PR now migrates the complete repository inventory of manual `??=` dynamic-import memoizers, preserving each call site's sticky-rejection or retry contract plus reset/peek behavior. Bundled plugins consume the helper through the public `openclaw/plugin-sdk/lazy-runtime` boundary.\n\nA repository guard now rejects newly introduced hand-written `??=` dynamic-import memoizers while leaving unrelated dynamic-import advisories informational.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get one lazy promise implementation instead of hundreds of repeated cache variables and loaders, with explicit APIs for retry, sticky rejection, inspection, and reset.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Complete inventory proof: `node scripts/check-dynamic-import-warts.mjs --fail-manual-memoizers` passes with zero manual `??=` dynamic-import memoizers.\n- Focused proof: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/shared/lazy-promise.test.ts src/shared/lazy-runtime.test.ts test/scripts/check-dynamic-import-warts.test.ts src/plugins/contracts/plugin-sdk-subpaths.test.ts` — 4 files, 39 tests passed across 3 shards.\n- Broader focused suites during migration — 455 additional tests passed across approval, lifecycle, gateway, SDK, tasks, status, and provider surfaces.\n- `pnpm build` — passed after rebasing onto current `main`, including CLI bootstrap, plugin SDK declaration/export checks, and UI build.\n- `pnpm check:import-cycles` — passed with 0 runtime value cycles.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwfs8tv6yfkwn73kv5jxeq9t` — full `check:changed` succeeded for the repository-wide migration. Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28548883955\n- Fresh Codex autoreview after the performance/packaging follow-up — clean, no accepted/actionable findings, 0.93 confidence.\n- Performance proof — cached loaders now return the exact cached promise instead of allocating an async wrapper promise per call.\n- Packaging proof — low-level promise helpers are no longer added to the public Plugin SDK; the SDK surface-budget tests pass, and the generated Code Mode declaration is restored from ~80 KB to 4,656 bytes.\n- Size proof — production code remains net-negative; full branch is +1,380/-2,347 lines, a net reduction of 967 lines.\n\n",
